\begin{justifying}
Spendemic is a full stack AI financial planning web application designed for international students studying in the United States. International students face a financial situation that is different from most domestic users of budgeting tools. They manage money across home and study currencies, work within visa based limits, handle irregular scholarship and family support, and plan around tuition, rent, travel, health insurance, and academic breaks. Spendemic addresses this gap through transaction tracking, category budgets, savings goals, multi currency support, visa work hour awareness, receipt uploads, CSV and Excel imports, a moderated student FAQ, an AI chat assistant, and probabilistic spending forecasts. The system uses a React and TypeScript frontend, a FastAPI and PostgreSQL backend, Google OAuth and email OTP authentication, Claude Haiku for assistant and import classification features, and a forecasting pipeline built around Amazon Chronos 2, Meta Prophet, and a statistical fallback model. The project demonstrates how AI can support practical student financial planning while still exposing the engineering trade offs required for authentication, deployment, model serving, data quality, and trust.
\end{justifying}

\noindent{Key Words: International students; Financial planning; Time series forecasting; Amazon Chronos 2; Full stack web application.}

