\chapter{Methodology}

This chapter describes the technical approach used to design and implement Spendemic. The methodology includes system architecture, mathematical formulation, algorithmic flow, data model design, backend API design, frontend architecture, forecasting design, AI assistant design, deployment, tools, hyperparameters, and evaluation metrics.

\section{System Architecture}

Spendemic follows a modular three tier architecture. The frontend is a React single page application built with TypeScript and Vite. The backend is a FastAPI application written in Python. The database is PostgreSQL, accessed through SQLAlchemy ORM and versioned with Alembic migrations. The frontend communicates with the backend through JSON based REST endpoints under the \texttt{/api/v1} prefix.

The frontend is deployed on Vercel. The backend is deployed on Render. PostgreSQL is provided by an external managed database service, currently Neon in the active deployment workflow. Chronos 2 inference is served locally during development and exposed to the deployed application through an ngrok tunnel when needed. This split architecture allows the application to demonstrate advanced model behavior without forcing the production backend to carry the full PyTorch and Chronos dependency load.


