\section{Strengths of the Current System}

The main strength of Spendemic is that the features are connected by a consistent domain model. The app does not only have transactions and a separate model. Transactions feed summaries. Settings feed forecast context. Jobs feed income. Forecast setup feeds reports. Budgets feed alerts. The assistant can understand navigation and financial profile context. The FAQ supports practical resources. This integration makes the application feel like a product rather than a collection of disconnected assignments.

Another strength is transparency. Many AI projects show an output without explaining the input. Spendemic makes missing fields, data sources, warnings, confidence bands, and factor drivers visible. This is important in financial planning, where users need to understand why a recommendation exists.

The third strength is graceful fallback. The application does not depend on a single ideal environment. If Chronos 2 is available, it can be used. If not, Prophet or the statistical fallback keeps the Reports page functional. This is practical engineering.

\section{Weaknesses of the Current System}

The current system still has weaknesses. The Chronos 2 model is not deployed as a permanent production service. OTP storage is in memory. Some compliance related weekly work hour data uses localStorage. Formal model evaluation results are not yet complete. The statistical fallback is intentionally simple. Some UI features depend on the quality of user entered forecast setup data.

These weaknesses do not invalidate the project. They define the next engineering steps. A project report should not pretend every part is complete. It should explain what works, what is limited, and what should be improved.


\section{Known Limitations}

\paragraph*{OTP Persistence.}

OTP codes are stored in process memory. If the backend restarts between OTP request and verification, the code is lost. Redis would be a better production solution.

\paragraph*{Visa Work Hours Local Storage.}

Some weekly visa work hour data is stored in localStorage. This works for a single browser but does not sync across devices. A backend endpoint would make this feature more reliable.

\paragraph*{Synthetic Anchors.}

The Chronos 2 covariate strategy is heuristic. It works as a practical bridge, but it is not the same as a true multivariate forecasting model.

\paragraph*{Loan Projection.}

The loan repayment projection is simplified and does not model interest. It is useful for basic payoff planning, but not for precise amortization.

